layful fall. The cat's body arcs slightly as it descends, its legs twitching in a relaxed manner. The camera continues its slight drift, keeping the focus on the interaction between the two subjects. The background remains plain white, with the soft lighting casting a faint shadow beneath <Subject 2> as it nears the ground. <Subject 1> watches the cat with a calm, attentive expression, her rolled-cuff jeans and white graphic t-shirt clearly visible in the soft light. The shot ends with <Subject 2> landing softly, its body still slightly arched, while <Subject 1> holds her pose, observing the cat's final position.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nQuiet room tone with a subtle, soft ambient hum that fades as the cat falls. The only distinct sound is the gentle, muffled thud of <Subject 2> landing on the ground, synchronized with the cat's final position in [Shot 2].\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nN/A","h3Summary":"Cat Gun · Send 2 · 608×320 · 5.17s · 1 refs","h3EditorProjectId":"f791edcd-5c2e-4f52-92cd-344e198ed286","h3SizeMode":"mp"},"widgets_values":["","subject_definitions:\n<Subject 1> is the anime-style young woman defined by <Picture 1>, with short brown hair and bangs, wearing a white graphic t-shirt and blue jeans with rolled cuffs.\n<Subject 2> is the long orange tabby cat defined by <Picture 1>, held horizontally across <Subject 1>'s body.\n\nsummary:\n[reference generation] <Subject 1> holds <Subject 2> in a grapple pose against a plain white background, then releases the cat into a slow, playful fall while the camera drifts slightly to mimic a human gaze.\n\nretention_analysis:\n<Subject 1> (appears in [Shot 1], [Shot 2]): partially_preserved - retain identity and clothing from <Picture 1>; change the pose from a static grapple to a release action.\n<Subject 2> (appears in [Shot 1], [Shot 2]): partially_preserved - retain identity and color from <Picture 1>; change the pose from being held horizontally to falling slowly.\n\ndetailed_description:\nAnime-style rendering wit